  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to the Ebola Epidemic Emergency &amp; Early Recovery in Sierra Leone - phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to continue to assist with the Ebola outbreak in Sierra Leone.

The outbreak of Ebola in Sierra Leone started on the 25th May 2014, from a single case in the Eastern District of Kailahun. On 30th. November 2014, we had a cumulative caseload of 5,712 infections, within a period of five months. 

Many NGOs continue to implement an excellent behaviour change campaign. Traditional and religious leaders have played their own part, but Ebola Virus Disease continues to ravage the entire country with unrelenting spikes in new cases just as we approach December when everyone expected a downward curve, which is particularly worrying. The persistently bleak daily updates only depict a depressing, shocking trajectory, showing that we have an uphill battle to find lasting solution to the serious humanitarian crisis as it unfolds in Sierra Leone.  This project is aimed at supporting the Diocesan Caritas through the National Caritas to address this emergency.</narrative>
  </description>
